{"id":"a19d7b6eacb882e0","group":"58","path":"58/batch15/58-df-markov-property.md","title":"Markov Property","display":"df-markov-property — Markov Property","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-markov-property","aliases":["58-df-markov-property","Markov Property"],"display":"df-markov-property — Markov Property","depends_on":["[[58-df-stochastic-process]]","[[58-df-sigma-algebra]]","[[58-df-function]]","[[58-df-conditional-expectation]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-markov-property"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-markov-property</span><span>Markov Property</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-markov-property — Markov Property"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"b5f77bed7dfe3f07\" href=\"?note=b5f77bed7dfe3f07\" title=\"58-df-stochastic-process\">58-df-stochastic-process</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"a740bdad87b97ac6\" href=\"?note=a740bdad87b97ac6\" title=\"58-df-sigma-algebra\">58-df-sigma-algebra</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"52ad543842bcb570\" href=\"?note=52ad543842bcb570\" title=\"58-df-conditional-expectation\">58-df-conditional-expectation</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\">\\((\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\)</span> (probability space)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(E,\\mathcal E)\">\\((E,\\mathcal E)\\)</span> (measurable state space)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\subseteq\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\">\\(T\\subseteq\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\)</span> (time set)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X:T\\to E^\\Omega\">\\(X:T\\to E^\\Omega\\)</span> (stochastic process)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal G:T\\to V\">\\(\\mathcal G:T\\to V\\)</span> (filtration)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{StochProc}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{StochProc}_S\\)</span> (stochastic-process predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"b5f77bed7dfe3f07\" href=\"?note=b5f77bed7dfe3f07\" title=\"58-df-stochastic-process\">58-df-stochastic-process</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}\">\\(\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"a740bdad87b97ac6\" href=\"?note=a740bdad87b97ac6\" title=\"58-df-sigma-algebra\">58-df-sigma-algebra</a> and <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{CondExp}_S(Y,Z,\\mathcal H,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\">\\(\\operatorname{CondExp}_S(Y,Z,\\mathcal H,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\)</span> (fully indexed conditional-expectation predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"52ad543842bcb570\" href=\"?note=52ad543842bcb570\" title=\"58-df-conditional-expectation\">58-df-conditional-expectation</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sigma_{\\Omega,\\mathcal E}(g)\">\\(\\sigma_{\\Omega,\\mathcal E}(g)\\)</span> (sigma-algebra generated by a measurable map <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"g:\\Omega\\to E\">\\(g:\\Omega\\to E\\)</span>, defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{FiltrationOn}_S(\\mathcal G,T,\\Omega,\\mathcal F)\">\\(\\mathrm{FiltrationOn}_S(\\mathcal G,T,\\Omega,\\mathcal F)\\)</span> (filtration predicate defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Markov}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Markov}_S\\)</span> (Markov-property predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}markov\\text{-}filtration}\\vdash \\mathrm{FiltrationOn}_S(\\mathcal G,T,\\Omega,\\mathcal F)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Function}(\\mathcal G,T,\\mathcal P(\\mathcal F))\\land\\forall t\\in T\\;\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}(\\mathcal G(t),\\Omega)\\land\\forall s,t\\in T\\;(s\\leq t\\to\\mathcal G(s)\\subseteq\\mathcal G(t))\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}markov\\text{-}filtration}\\vdash \\mathrm{FiltrationOn}_S(\\mathcal G,T,\\Omega,\\mathcal F)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Function}(\\mathcal G,T,\\mathcal P(\\mathcal F))\\land\\forall t\\in T\\;\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}(\\mathcal G(t),\\Omega)\\land\\forall s,t\\in T\\;(s\\leq t\\to\\mathcal G(s)\\subseteq\\mathcal G(t))\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}markov\\text{-}generated\\text{-}sigma}\\vdash \\mathrm{Function}(g,\\Omega,E)\\land\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}(\\mathcal E,E)\\to\\sigma_{\\Omega,\\mathcal E}(g)\\coloneqq\\sigma_\\Omega\\!\\left(\\{g^{-1}[B]:B\\in\\mathcal E\\}\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}markov\\text{-}generated\\text{-}sigma}\\vdash \\mathrm{Function}(g,\\Omega,E)\\land\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}(\\mathcal E,E)\\to\\sigma_{\\Omega,\\mathcal E}(g)\\coloneqq\\sigma_\\Omega\\!\\left(\\{g^{-1}[B]:B\\in\\mathcal E\\}\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}markov\\text{-}property} \\vdash \\mathrm{Markov}_S(X,\\mathcal G,T,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,E,\\mathcal E)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{StochProc}_S(X,T,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,E,\\mathcal E)\\land\\mathrm{FiltrationOn}_S(\\mathcal G,T,\\Omega,\\mathcal F)\\land\\forall t\\in T\\;(\\sigma_{\\Omega,\\mathcal E}(X(t))\\subseteq\\mathcal G(t))\\land\\forall s,t\\in T\\;\\left(s&lt;t\\to\\forall B\\in\\mathcal E\\;\\exists Y,Z\\in\\mathbb R^\\Omega\\;\\left(\\operatorname{CondExp}_S(Y,\\mathbf 1_B\\circ X(t),\\mathcal G(s),\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\land\\operatorname{CondExp}_S(Z,\\mathbf 1_B\\circ X(t),\\sigma_{\\Omega,\\mathcal E}(X(s)),\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\land\\mathbb P(\\{\\omega\\in\\Omega:Y(\\omega)\\neq Z(\\omega)\\})=0\\right)\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}markov\\text{-}property} \\vdash \\mathrm{Markov}_S(X,\\mathcal G,T,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,E,\\mathcal E)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{StochProc}_S(X,T,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,E,\\mathcal E)\\land\\mathrm{FiltrationOn}_S(\\mathcal G,T,\\Omega,\\mathcal F)\\land\\forall t\\in T\\;(\\sigma_{\\Omega,\\mathcal E}(X(t))\\subseteq\\mathcal G(t))\\land\\forall s,t\\in T\\;\\left(s&lt;t\\to\\forall B\\in\\mathcal E\\;\\exists Y,Z\\in\\mathbb R^\\Omega\\;\\left(\\operatorname{CondExp}_S(Y,\\mathbf 1_B\\circ X(t),\\mathcal G(s),\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\land\\operatorname{CondExp}_S(Z,\\mathbf 1_B\\circ X(t),\\sigma_{\\Omega,\\mathcal E}(X(s)),\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\land\\mathbb P(\\{\\omega\\in\\Omega:Y(\\omega)\\neq Z(\\omega)\\})=0\\right)\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The definition states that, conditionally on the present state, the conditional law of a future state does not depend on the earlier filtration.</li>\n<li>Adaptedness is included explicitly by <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sigma(X(t))\\subseteq\\mathcal G(t)\">\\(\\sigma(X(t))\\subseteq\\mathcal G(t)\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Conditional expectations carry the full probability-space signature, and the natural sigma-algebra is explicitly generated from measurable preimages.</li>\n<li>Strong Markov at stopping times and Chapman-Kolmogorov identities are theorem-level consequences under their additional hypotheses.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Norris, Markov Chains</li>\n<li>Ethier and Kurtz, Markov Processes</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-stochastic-process","status":"resolved","id":"b5f77bed7dfe3f07","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-stochastic-process]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-sigma-algebra","status":"resolved","id":"a740bdad87b97ac6","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-sigma-algebra]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-function]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-conditional-expectation","status":"resolved","id":"52ad543842bcb570","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-conditional-expectation]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-stochastic-process","status":"resolved","id":"b5f77bed7dfe3f07","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{StochProc}_S$ (stochastic-process predicate, see [[58-df-stochastic-process]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-sigma-algebra","status":"resolved","id":"a740bdad87b97ac6","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}$ and $\\mathrm{Function}$ (see [[58-df-sigma-algebra]] and [[58-df-function]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}$ and $\\mathrm{Function}$ (see [[58-df-sigma-algebra]] and [[58-df-function]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-conditional-expectation","status":"resolved","id":"52ad543842bcb570","anchor":"ref-8","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{CondExp}_S(Y,Z,\\mathcal H,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)$ (fully indexed conditional-expectation predicate, see [[58-df-conditional-expectation]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)","display":false},{"tex":"(E,\\mathcal E)","display":false},{"tex":"T\\subseteq\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}","display":false},{"tex":"X:T\\to E^\\Omega","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal G:T\\to V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{StochProc}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{CondExp}_S(Y,Z,\\mathcal H,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)","display":false},{"tex":"\\sigma_{\\Omega,\\mathcal E}(g)","display":false},{"tex":"g:\\Omega\\to E","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{FiltrationOn}_S(\\mathcal G,T,\\Omega,\\mathcal F)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Markov}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}markov\\text{-}filtration}\\vdash \\mathrm{FiltrationOn}_S(\\mathcal G,T,\\Omega,\\mathcal F)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Function}(\\mathcal G,T,\\mathcal P(\\mathcal F))\\land\\forall t\\in T\\;\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}(\\mathcal G(t),\\Omega)\\land\\forall s,t\\in T\\;(s\\leq t\\to\\mathcal G(s)\\subseteq\\mathcal G(t))","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}markov\\text{-}generated\\text{-}sigma}\\vdash \\mathrm{Function}(g,\\Omega,E)\\land\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}(\\mathcal E,E)\\to\\sigma_{\\Omega,\\mathcal E}(g)\\coloneqq\\sigma_\\Omega\\!\\left(\\{g^{-1}[B]:B\\in\\mathcal E\\}\\right)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}markov\\text{-}property} \\vdash \\mathrm{Markov}_S(X,\\mathcal G,T,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,E,\\mathcal E)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{StochProc}_S(X,T,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,E,\\mathcal E)\\land\\mathrm{FiltrationOn}_S(\\mathcal G,T,\\Omega,\\mathcal F)\\land\\forall t\\in T\\;(\\sigma_{\\Omega,\\mathcal E}(X(t))\\subseteq\\mathcal G(t))\\land\\forall s,t\\in T\\;\\left(s<t\\to\\forall B\\in\\mathcal E\\;\\exists Y,Z\\in\\mathbb R^\\Omega\\;\\left(\\operatorname{CondExp}_S(Y,\\mathbf 1_B\\circ X(t),\\mathcal G(s),\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\land\\operatorname{CondExp}_S(Z,\\mathbf 1_B\\circ X(t),\\sigma_{\\Omega,\\mathcal E}(X(s)),\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\land\\mathbb P(\\{\\omega\\in\\Omega:Y(\\omega)\\neq Z(\\omega)\\})=0\\right)\\right)","display":true},{"tex":"\\sigma(X(t))\\subseteq\\mathcal G(t)","display":false}],"bytes":3146,"backlinks":[{"id":"6c6a1de6afbc3124","anchor":"ref-2","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Markov}_S\\subseteq V^8$ (see [[../batch15/58-df-markov-property.md]])"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-819","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-df-markov-property.md|58-df-markov-property]]（batch15）"}],"outgoing":["b5f77bed7dfe3f07","a740bdad87b97ac6","36d7463d215be751","52ad543842bcb570"]}